ernal Error ()\nciteturn1470view3 [wordlim: 200] Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1469view3\",\"id\":4}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://www.cacb.uscourts.gov/sites/cacb/files/documents/forms/F3015-1.04DORDERPPATTACH.docx: (400) Unsupported content-type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn1470view4 [wordlim: 200] Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1469view4\",\"id\":3}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://www.cacb.uscourts.gov/sites/cacb/files/documents/forms/F4003-2.1AVOIDLIENRPORDER.docx: (400) Unsupported content-type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.cacb.uscourts.gov/sites/cacb/files/documents/forms/F4003-2.2AVOIDLIENPPMOTION.pdf)\nciteturn1470view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 7; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1469view5\",\"id\":3}); Total lines: 283\nL0@P0: “Bankruptcy Code” and “11 U.S.C.” refer to the United States Bankruptcy Code, Title 11 of the United States Code.\nL1@P0: “FRBP” refers to the Federal Rules of Bankruptcy Procedure. “LBR” and “LBRs” refer to the Local Bankruptcy Rule(s) of this court.\nL2@P0: This form is mandatory. It has been approved for use by the United States Bankruptcy Court for the Central District of California.\nL3@P0: December 2017 Page 1 F 4003-2.2.AVOID.LIEN.PP.MOTION\nL4@P0: Attorney or Party Name, Address, Telephone & FAX\nL5@P0: Numbers, State Bar Number & Email Address\nL6@P0: FOR COURT USE ONLY\nL7@P0: Debtor appearing without attorney\nL8@P0: Attorney for:\nL9@P0: UNITED STATES BANKRUPTCY COURT\nL10@P0: CENTRAL DISTRICT OF CALIFORNIA - DIVISION\nL11@P0: In re:\nL12@P0: D\nL13@P0: Debtor(s).\nL14@P0: CASE NUMBER:\nL15@P0: CHAPTER:\nL16@P0: DEBTOR’S NOTICE OF MOTION\nL17@P0: AND MOTION TO AVOID LIEN UNDER\nL18@P0: 11 U.S.C. § 522(f) AND, IF APPLICABLE,\nL19@P0: FOR TURNOVER OF PROPERTY\nL20@P0: (PERSONAL PROPERTY)\nL21@P0: [No hearing required unless\nL22@P0: requested under LBR 9013-1(o)]\nL23@P0: Creditor Name:\nL24@P0: TO THE CREDITOR, CREDITOR'S ATTORNEY AND OTHER INTERESTED PARTIES:\nL25@P0: 1. NOTICE IS GIVEN that Debtor moves this court for an order, pursuant to LBR 9013-1(o) upon notice of opportunity to\nL26@P0: request a hearing (i.e., without a hearing unless requested), (1) avoiding a lien on the personal property (Personal\nL27@P0: Property) described herein on the grounds set forth below and (2) directing turnover of the Personal Property to\nL28@P0: Debtor, if applicable.\nL29@P0: 2. Deadline for Opposition Papers:\nL30@P0: Pursuant to LBR 9013-1(o), any party opposing Debtor's motion may file and serve a written opposition and request a\nL31@P0: hearing on this motion. If you fail to file a written response within 14 days of the date of service of this notice, plus 3\nL32@P0: additional days if you were served by mail or pursuant to Federal Rules of Civil Procedure 5(b)(2)(D) or (F), the court\nL33@P0: may treat such failure as a waiver of your right to oppose this motion and may grant the requested relief.\nL34@P0: 3. Type of case:\nL35@P0: a. A voluntary petition under Chapter 7 11 12 13 was filed on: ______________\nL36@P0: b. An involuntary petition under Chapter 7 11 was filed on: _______________\nL37@P0-1: An order for relief under Chapter 7 11 was entered on: _____________This form is mandatory. It has been approved for use in the United States Bankruptcy Court for the Central District of California.\nL38@P1: December 2017 Page 2 F 4003-2.2.AVOID.LIEN.PP.MOTION\nL39@P1: c. An order of conversion to Chapter 7 11 12 13 was filed on: ______________\nL40@P1: d. Other: _____________________________\nL41@P1: 4. Procedural Status:\nL42@P1: a. Name of Trustee appointed (if any): _________________________________\nL43@P1: b. Name of Attorney for Trustee (if any): ______________________________\nL44@P1: 5. Debtor claims an exemption in the subject Personal Property under:\nL45@P1: a. California Code of Civil Procedure § exemption amount claimed on schedules:\nL46@P1: $ ______________\nL47@P1: b. California Code of Civil Procedure § exemption amount claimed on schedules:\nL48@P1: $ ________________\nL49@P1: c. Other statute (specify): _________________________________________________________\nL50@P1: d. Other statute (specify): _________________________________________________________\nL51@P1: 6. Debtor's entitlement to an exemption is impaired by:\nL52@P1: a. A judicial lien, other than a judicial lien that secures a debt of a kind that is specified in 11 U.S.C. § 523(a)(5)\nL53@P1: (domestic support obligations).\nL54@P1: b. A nonpossessory, nonpurchase-money security interest , the details of which are as follows:\nL55@P1: (1) On (specify date): __________ Debtor obtained a loan from Creditor in the principal amount of (specify\nL56@P1: amount): $ _____________\nL57@P1: (2) As security for said loan, Debtor gave Creditor a security interest in the Personal Property in Debtor's\nL58@P1: possession.\nL59@P1: (3) The loan was neither obtained nor used for the purpose of buying the Personal Property.\nL60@P1: (4) The current balance due on the loan is (specify amount): $ _________________\nL61@P1: (5) The Personal Property is one or more of the types of personal property listed in 11 U.S.C.\nL62@P1: § 522(f)(1)(B)(i), (ii), and (iii) (household furnishings, tools of the trade of the debtor, prescribed health\nL63@P1: aids for the debtor, household goods as defined in 11 U.S.C. § 522(f)(4), etc.).\nL64@P1: 7. On Schedule C to Debtor’s bankruptcy petition, Debtor claimed an exemption in this Personal Property.\nL65@P1: 8. Debtor alleges that the fair market value of each individual item of the Personal Property claimed exempt is set forth in\nL66@P1: a declaration attached here